        "pwm_output",
        "led_high"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_LED (also aliased D25) — onboard status LED, active-high. Confirmed present on GPIO25 via this board's own pins_arduino.h (PIN_LED define, matching the upstream earlephilhower/arduino-pico source verbatim), an independent third-party setup guide (nwgat.ninja/rp2040-lora/) and a Raspberry Pi forum thread both citing Waveshare's own LED_PIN=25 example code, and the Waveshare wiki's own ping-pong LoRa demo description of the onboard LED blinking on receive. digital_input dropped to match this repo's established led_high precedent for dedicated onboard LED pins; pwm_output kept since arduino-pico's analogWrite() works on any RP2040 GPIO, enabling brightness dimming."
    },
